{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Assess the resolution and recurrence protection for each target, with an evidence-backed behavioral verdict. Pass only when the repair is supported; block or defer when it is not. Diagnosis alone is insufficient. Additional caller focus: Re-review the whole repaired surface after blocker findings. Confirm test-compatibility-only is now mechanically bounded, all seven producer migrations and standing gate wiring are present, and identify only remaining code blockers.","packet_sha256":"2d81e0bcdbf5bbea70c6b9ef0e8c76d18d44aa709a02e9c4ea979a0d0dd409ae","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"599faf40a83a709169447e4c53d9e9fa013a4304fa92c1211843f56ac3c80387","verdict":"pass","target_observations":[{"target":"corca-ai/charness#813","verdict":"pass","summary":"The repaired surface provides receipt-bound ownership for all seven identified directory producers, mechanically restricts the test-compatibility-only exemption, and installs the inventory check as a standing quality gate. No remaining code blocker is evident in the bound input.","evidence":["The seven migrated producer identities are represented by the Claude evaluator home plus owned child directories in check-links-internal, check-markdown, check-python-lint, both check-secrets paths, and check-shell; their manifest dispositions are owned-scratch.","scripts/run_quality_engine_runtime.py opens an OwnedScratch owner and explicitly passes CHARNESS_OWNED_SCRATCH_ROOT to child gates; scripts/exported-copy-guard.sh gives standalone gates the receipt-backed run_owned_scratch_command.py adapter and isolates concurrent children beneath invocation-local roots.","scripts/agent-runtime/run-local-eval-test.mjs either nests the Claude home beneath an inherited owned root or creates a temporaryOwnedRuntimeHome with receipt lifecycle cleanup.","scripts/gates/check_temp_producer_inventory.py permits test-compatibility-only directory classifications only when the detected stable identity is present in the executable TEST_COMPAT_DIRECTORY_IDENTITIES allowlist; a manifest row alone cannot select the exemption.","The inventory validator fails missing, stale, raw unowned-directory, invalid compatibility, parse-error, path mismatch, symbol mismatch, and incorrect owned-directory disposition cases.","tests/test_temp_producer_inventory.py includes negative controls for unregistered, missing, stale, and unauthorized test-compatibility-only producers, plus process-bound success, failure, timeout, and cancellation checks for the standalone ownership adapter.",".agents/quality-gates.yaml wires check-temp-producer-inventory into the standard main phase with --require-git-file-listing, making recurrence detection part of the standing gate surface.","Parent-supplied execution evidence reports a complete 47/47 inventory, focused tests, full release gates, and a changed-line clean run."]}],"findings":[],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The compatibility fallback in exported-copy-guard.sh creates a repo-local compatibility root when the receipt adapter is absent.","bin":"bounded non-blocker","disposition":"The branch is mechanically conditioned on the adapter being absent and is documented for deliberately minimal gate fixtures; production source and packaged surfaces are expected to carry the adapter, while the manifest cannot independently grant this exemption."},{"concern":"The packet does not contain raw output from the reported inventory and gate executions.","bin":"packet limitation","disposition":"Execution is explicitly parent-supplied evidence under the review instructions. The bound code and tests support the behavioral claims, but this review does not independently authenticate those runs."},{"concern":"Abrupt machine loss or kernel SIGKILL may prevent producer-local cleanup.","bin":"explicit non-claim","disposition":"This does not defeat the repair: receipt ownership makes orphan inspection and recovery possible, and the spec expressly avoids claiming external-tool cleanup under those conditions."}],"next_move":"Approval is supported for corca-ai/charness#813; retain the inventory gate and its executable compatibility allowlist as the recurrence boundary.","non_claims":["This review did not execute the reported 47/47 inventory, focused tests, release gates, or changed-line coverage run.","This review judged only the identity-bound inline semantic payload and did not infer additional behavior from the current workspace.","This review does not claim cleanup under machine loss or kernel SIGKILL; it claims attributable receipt state and bounded recovery.","Goal evidence lineage is not goal-bound."]}
